# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployed separately. ifc-graphx/ is its own git repository with its own
# GitHub remote (github.com/ashwin-ned/ifc-graphx) and its own CI -- pushing
# it here would create a nested-repo mess and duplicate a live deployment.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
ifc-graphx/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored external tools, each with its own .git history (Ifc2Graph, IFC2SB).
# Re-clone from the upstream URLs in README.md rather than duplicating their
# history here; committing them would also turn nested .git dirs into
# accidental gitlinks.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/

# Staged deletions under manual review -- never meant to be published.
TO-DELETE/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw corpora. Multiple gigabytes; individual real IFC files run up to 70 MB
# (dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/model_126.ifc, model_152.ifc), well past what
# a plain git history should carry with no Git LFS configured. Regenerate or
# re-download per the Data section of README.md:
#   - real IFC + floorplans: supplied dataset, not redistributable here
#   - synthetic IFC + ground truth: main/generate_building.py (deterministic,
#     --seed0 0 reproduces the archived corpus exactly -- verified 18 Sep 2026)
#   - damaged synthetic levels: main/damage_ifc.py
#   - blind-rendered vision corpus: main/render_blind.py (~2 min for the
#     real corpus once the .plan.json extraction below exists)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/*.ifc
dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/floorplans/
dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/vision/
dataset/test_set/*.ifc
# The partner dataset is 236 MB and turned out to be almost entirely the
# per-model scene-graph JSONs (208 files, ~1.1 MB each), not .ifc -- an
# .ifc-only exclusion here missed the actual bulk of it on the first pass.
dataset/BIM-GNI-Ramblr/**/*.json
dataset/BIM-GNI-Ramblr/**/*.ifc
dataset/synthetic_data/*/*.ifc
dataset/synthetic_data/*/floorplans/
dataset/synthetic_data/*/vision/

# Excluded by file TYPE above, not by whole directory -- a whole-directory
# ignore (e.g. `dataset/synthetic_data/synth150/`) would also hide anything
# git is later told to keep inside it, since git never looks inside an
# ignored directory in the first place. Kept as a result:
#   - corpus.manifest.json (a few KB each): the size/SHA-256 record
#     main/verify_corpus.py checks against
#   - *.gt.json (604 KB for all of synth150): the deterministic ground truth
#     this project's reproducibility claim rests on -- regenerating it
#     exactly (main/generate_building.py --seed0 0) is verified, but 604 KB
#     is cheap enough to just keep rather than lean on that every time
#   - dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/plans/*.plan.json (9.4 MB): the extracted
#     topology the whole method runs on, too useful to force a re-parse of
#     2 GB of IFC for
#   - dataset/BIM-GNI-Ramblr/*.md: the partner dataset's own verification doc
!dataset/2025_BIMfundamentals/plans/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regeneratable intermediate outputs: per-building graph dumps for every
# (corpus x damage level x method) cell -- results/baselines/ alone is 68 MB
# of files main/baselines.py + main/eval_connectivity.py reproduce on demand.
# The small SUMMARY score files one level up (results/bl_*.json,
# *.manifest.json) are kept -- those are what README.md and the report cite.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/baselines/
results/bl_synthetic_L2/
results/bl_synthetic_L3/
results/bl_synthetic_L4/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standard
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.bak

# LaTeX build artifacts (the report itself -- .tex and .pdf -- is tracked).
report/*.aux
report/*.log
report/*.out
report/*.toc
report/*.fls
report/*.fdb_latexmk
